   "transcript_text": "person_1 (DOCTOR) 388.63-389.63s: okay, noted\nperson_1 (DOCTOR) 390.92-394.55s: Right, let me check a few things physically.\nperson_1 (DOCTOR) 395.42-397.40s: Let me just check something.\nperson_1 (DOCTOR) 414.18-419.74s: There's a small scab where the cut was, no pus coming out.\nperson_1 (DOCTOR) 420.57-423.07s: just relax, I'll be quick\nperson_1 (DOCTOR) 438.27-446.68s: The skin on the lower leg is red, warm and swollen, about the size of my palm.\nperson_1 (DOCTOR) 451.65-479.90s: so, good, that's the examination. Let's book blood tests to look into infection. Let's book a wound swab to look into infected wound. I'd like you to take clindamycin, 300 milligrams, three times a day, for seven days. That should help with skin infection. Mark the edge of the redness with a pen so we can see whether it spreads. Keep the leg raised on a pillow when you're sitting",
